<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5016" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">băsĭliscus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλίσκος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of lizard</i>, <i>a
			basilisk</i>: Lacerta basiliscus, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 8,
				21, 33, § 78 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App.
				Herb. 128</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sol. 27, 50</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Psa. 90</span></i> (91), 13. —For the deriv. of the word
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεύς</span> (king), v. <i><span class="en">Luc. 9,
			726</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A surname of</i> Cn. Pompeius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 11, §
		25</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
